  "final_answer": "Field coverage is complete. I successfully found the answer.\n\n## Answer\n\nI searched the Amazon Kindle Store for English-language books on Roman Empire history, sorted by newest arrivals. Applying the \"Coming Soon\" filter (which shows upcoming releases in ascending date order), I found the following book that will be released within a month from today (September 17, 2026):\n\n### 📖 Mastering the Body: Daily Life, Inequality, and Slavery in Roman Homes and Society\n\n- **Title:** Mastering the Body: Daily Life, Inequality, and Slavery in Roman Homes and Society\n- **Author:** F. Mira Green\n- **Release Date:** October 15, 2026 (28 days from today — within one month)\n- **Format/Price:** Kindle Edition — $24.99 (also available in Hardcover $145.00 and Paperback $34.95)\n- **Publisher:** Cornell University Press\n- **Language:** English\n- **Print Length:** 238 pages\n- **URL:** https://www.amazon.com/Mastering-Body-Inequality-Slavery-Society-ebook/dp/B0H9ZWCP5Y\n\nThis book offers an innovative exploration of the intimate, bodily routines that shaped—and were shaped by—Roman society, drawing on archaeological evidence from Pompeii and Herculaneum and works from Latin authors like Seneca, Juvenal, and Apuleius to examine how dietary habits and domestic labor reinforced hierarchies and power structures in Roman households.",
